<title>UK: DSL Bank sets 1.5 billion mark 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>DSL Bank sets 1.5 billion mark 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, Banque Nationale de Paris and Dresdner Kleinwort Benson.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE SIEDLUNGS-UND LANDESRENTENBANK</p>
<p> AMT    1.5 BLN DEM   COUPON     5.625     MATURITY    13.AUG.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  102.10    PAY DATE    13.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  3.00	REOFFER    99.425    SPREAD	+13 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FRANKFURT PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> IBCA	 AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS US/GB/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.325     SELL CONC  2.175     LISTING FEE 0.50</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.00 PCT BUND DUE JUL.07</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
